{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And what livestock you had with me</b> — the reckoning of the small amount of your livestock that came into my hand, how much it was. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 30:29). That is, you know how much your livestock was when it came with me. And it would be more fitting to say, 'And your livestock that was with me — you know,' for 'little you had before I came, and it burst forth to abundance' (Genesis 30:30). Or we may interpret: 'You know what I have served you,' for with all my strength I labored, and you know what your livestock was with me, for they are many days, and you know that 'little you had before me and it burst forth to abundance' beyond the way of all the land — only it was the blessing of YHWH that came from the time my foot entered your house. And this is the correct interpretation."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The Hebrew behind 'for they are many days' (כי ימים רבים הם) is slightly awkward; translated hyper-literally as Ramban's compressed syntax suggests, alluding to Jacob's long years of service."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:58.083415220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}